WEBVTT

00:00:46.567 --> 00:00:47.525
Tony.

00:00:47.568 --> 00:00:49.396
Gena Marino,

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:51.659
my seventh grade
geology teacher?

00:00:51.703 --> 00:00:53.183
Wh-What are you doing in space?

00:00:53.226 --> 00:00:55.141
And in a revealing toga?

00:00:55.185 --> 00:00:56.969
Don't worry
about all that, Tony.

00:00:57.012 --> 00:00:59.406
Come here,
let me brush your hair.

00:00:59.450 --> 00:01:02.017
You can tell me about that
race car novel you're writing.

00:01:03.193 --> 00:01:04.498
Oh, my gosh. I've never

00:01:04.542 --> 00:01:06.239
told anyone about that.

00:01:06.283 --> 00:01:08.154
I wrote myself in
as the main character.

00:01:08.198 --> 00:01:09.677
His name's Speedy McWheels.

00:01:09.721 --> 00:01:12.724
So clever. Tell me more.

00:02:33.326 --> 00:02:36.938
&lt;i&gt;Captain's log,
stardate 58256.2.&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:36.982 --> 00:02:38.984
&lt;i&gt;Jengus IV is a remote planet&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:39.027 --> 00:02:40.986
&lt;i&gt;which was believed
to be uninhabited&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:41.029 --> 00:02:43.771
&lt;i&gt;until indigenous silicate
creatures, called the Scrubble,&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:43.815 --> 00:02:47.079
&lt;i&gt;started turning Federation
scientists into statues.&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:47.122 --> 00:02:49.342
&lt;i&gt;Captain Murakami
of the USS&lt;/i&gt; Hood

00:02:49.386 --> 00:02:52.606
&lt;i&gt;answered the distress call
and brokered tentative peace.&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:53.912 --> 00:02:55.827
&lt;i&gt;With the conflict resolved,&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:55.870 --> 00:02:57.437
&lt;i&gt;the&lt;/i&gt; Cerritos &lt;i&gt;and the&lt;/i&gt; Carlsbad &lt;i&gt;
are coordinating&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:57.481 --> 00:02:59.613
&lt;i&gt;to relocate the outpost.&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:59.657 --> 00:03:01.441
Once again,
we're cleaning up a mess

00:03:01.485 --> 00:03:03.138
for a bunch
of outpost scientists.

00:03:03.182 --> 00:03:05.402
You know why these guys
are always getting eaten,

00:03:05.445 --> 00:03:07.621
disappearing, or getting eggs
laid in their chest?

00:03:07.665 --> 00:03:09.580
'Cause they're working
on the frontier?

00:03:09.623 --> 00:03:12.104
Because they're weirdos.
You want to explore space?

00:03:12.147 --> 00:03:13.801
Join Starfleet,
go to the Academy.

00:03:13.845 --> 00:03:15.803
But no, that's too much effort.

00:03:15.847 --> 00:03:17.327
They just got to get
their degrees

00:03:17.370 --> 00:03:19.242
in studying spores or whatever,

00:03:19.285 --> 00:03:21.679
then head off into the quadrant
and get devoured by a plant!

00:03:21.722 --> 00:03:23.681
Is this a mission briefing
or a stand-up routine?

00:03:23.724 --> 00:03:26.814
Oh, no, no. His stand-up's
more a raw, unfiltered take

00:03:26.858 --> 00:03:29.077
- on dating and mating.

00:03:29.121 --> 00:03:31.558
Anyway, now that the Scrubble
and the scientists have agreed

00:03:31.602 --> 00:03:34.692
not to attack each other, it's
our job to set up a new base

00:03:34.735 --> 00:03:36.259
and remove these.

00:03:36.302 --> 00:03:38.348
Psychic mines--
they read your thoughts

00:03:38.391 --> 00:03:41.046
and bring your fantasies
to life, then turn you to stone.

00:03:41.089 --> 00:03:43.091
Be careful down there.

00:03:43.135 --> 00:03:45.616
Captain wants us to look good
in front of the &lt;i&gt;Carlsbad&lt;/i&gt; crew.

00:03:45.659 --> 00:03:47.705
Cali-class gets real gossipy.

00:03:47.748 --> 00:03:50.055
Glad to see that our priorities
are in the right place.

00:03:50.098 --> 00:03:52.579
Just follow Stevens's orders
like they were coming from me.

00:03:52.623 --> 00:03:55.930
Because we're best friends,
and we share a sacred bond.

00:03:55.974 --> 00:03:57.845
Dismissed.

00:03:57.889 --> 00:04:00.979
You have to stop saying
that we have a sacred bond.

00:04:01.022 --> 00:04:03.634
I feel it, sir,
and I know you do, too.

00:04:03.677 --> 00:04:05.026
Ooh, Tendi, we're heading

00:04:05.070 --> 00:04:06.811
down to the planet
to move a bunch of rocks.

00:04:06.854 --> 00:04:08.639
Ah, that's so cool.
Wish I could join,

00:04:08.682 --> 00:04:11.772
but I'm starting my senior
science officer training today.

00:04:11.816 --> 00:04:14.253
Whoa, look at you,
getting all bridge-ready.

00:04:14.297 --> 00:04:16.037
I've been
prepping so much,

00:04:16.081 --> 00:04:18.213
I'm afraid my brain's
gonna explode with science.

00:04:18.257 --> 00:04:20.303
Ah, that's how I want to go.

00:04:20.346 --> 00:04:23.001
All right, I'm off to find out
who my senior officer mentor is.

00:04:23.044 --> 00:04:24.002
Wish me luck.

00:04:24.045 --> 00:04:26.744
Wait, no, wish me facts.

00:04:28.963 --> 00:04:31.923
- Ah, Ensign, join me.
- Hey, Dr. Migleemo.

00:04:31.966 --> 00:04:33.794
Sorry, I don't have
time to chat.

00:04:33.838 --> 00:04:35.274
I'm actually meeting my mentor

00:04:35.318 --> 00:04:36.928
for senior science
officer training.

00:04:36.971 --> 00:04:39.147
Well, I wonder
who that could be. It's me.

00:04:39.191 --> 00:04:41.454
-  'Tis I.
- Wait, what?

00:04:41.498 --> 00:04:43.543
Through the strange alchemy
of command,

00:04:43.587 --> 00:04:46.111
the task of mentoring you
has fallen to me.

00:04:46.154 --> 00:04:47.808
Now grab a seat
and let's get started.

00:04:47.852 --> 00:04:50.202
Oh, and do help yourself
to some of these

00:04:50.245 --> 00:04:53.553
Corvarian sludge worms.
They are exquisitely charred.

00:04:53.597 --> 00:04:56.513
Oh. G-Great.
-  Mmm!

00:05:05.304 --> 00:05:06.479
Lieutenant Commander Stevens?

00:05:06.523 --> 00:05:08.089
Ensign Kearns reporting.

00:05:08.133 --> 00:05:09.874
We're here to provide assistance
from the &lt;i&gt;Carlsbad.&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:09.917 --> 00:05:13.312
Great. You guys'll dismantle and
relocate the outpost equipment.

00:05:13.356 --> 00:05:14.531
&lt;i&gt;Cerritos,&lt;/i&gt; you're gonna clear

00:05:14.574 --> 00:05:16.402
the area of fantasy rocks,

00:05:16.446 --> 00:05:18.230
which are still live,
so be careful.

00:05:18.273 --> 00:05:20.580
Uh, what do we do
if our fantasies appear?

00:05:20.624 --> 00:05:23.670
Well, they should dissipate
after a few hours,

00:05:23.714 --> 00:05:26.151
but if anything
should try to tempt you,

00:05:26.194 --> 00:05:28.632
you know, think about
parrises squares.

00:05:28.675 --> 00:05:30.111
What up, 'badders?

00:05:30.155 --> 00:05:31.635
I'm Mariner,
that's Rutherford, and this

00:05:31.678 --> 00:05:33.506
little bird-boned
fella is Boimler.

00:05:33.550 --> 00:05:35.160
Uh, yeah, we know who you are.

00:05:35.203 --> 00:05:37.205
Everyone's heard
about the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos.&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:37.249 --> 00:05:38.816
Oh, um, cool?

00:05:38.859 --> 00:05:41.035
Oh, hey, you guys were just
at Pellex II, right?

00:05:41.079 --> 00:05:42.472
Did you get a chance
to sneak over

00:05:42.515 --> 00:05:44.082
to the old Pleasure Festival?

00:05:44.125 --> 00:05:47.215
No, we were aboard our ship,
following orders.

00:05:47.259 --> 00:05:49.043
We do not sneak.

00:05:49.087 --> 00:05:51.176
Yeah, no, I just meant, uh...
Look, I don't sneak either.

00:05:51.219 --> 00:05:52.612
I-I didn't mean sneak.
I just meant, like...

00:05:52.656 --> 00:05:54.266
Uh, i-it's gonna be
a slog today.

00:05:54.309 --> 00:05:55.398
If you guys get sick
of dismantling the station,

00:05:55.441 --> 00:05:56.877
we can always switch it up.

00:05:56.921 --> 00:05:59.227
Uh-huh. Hey, Cor'dee,
is "switching it up"

00:05:59.271 --> 00:06:01.447
- in our mission parameters?
- It is not.

00:06:01.491 --> 00:06:03.884
And why are we wasting time
with all this talk?

00:06:03.928 --> 00:06:06.409
- Uh, well, I just, I...
- Eh, look, we've heard about how

00:06:06.452 --> 00:06:10.108
you do things on the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos.&lt;/i&gt;
We're not here to screw around.

00:06:11.283 --> 00:06:13.067
What the hell's their problem?

00:06:13.111 --> 00:06:14.895
They were acting like
the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos&lt;/i&gt; was a joke.

00:06:14.939 --> 00:06:16.593
Do we have a reputation?

00:06:16.636 --> 00:06:18.682
I don't know. Look, we should
probably get to work.

00:06:23.774 --> 00:06:25.732
&lt;i&gt;
So, have you ever&lt;/i&gt;

00:06:25.776 --> 00:06:27.342
trained a science
officer before?

00:06:27.386 --> 00:06:30.737
Absolutely... not, no.

00:06:30.781 --> 00:06:32.217
I didn't know they did this.

00:06:32.260 --> 00:06:34.175
But Starfleet sent along
a lovely manual,

00:06:34.219 --> 00:06:35.568
which I have been skimming,

00:06:35.612 --> 00:06:38.049
so you and I will be
learning together.

00:06:38.092 --> 00:06:39.093
Now, isn't that fun?

00:06:39.137 --> 00:06:40.486
Sure is.

00:06:40.530 --> 00:06:42.488
Now, let's see here.

00:06:42.532 --> 00:06:45.317
Table of contents. Good start.
Foreword by Ambassador Spock.

00:06:45.360 --> 00:06:48.320
Hmm, not bad. Okay,
Vulcan stuff, Vulcan stuff,

00:06:48.363 --> 00:06:50.540
Vulcan stuff... I tell you what,
it would've been logical

00:06:50.583 --> 00:06:52.106
- to find an editor.
- Just so you know,

00:06:52.150 --> 00:06:53.673
I've been studying super hard. Microbiology,

00:06:53.717 --> 00:06:55.936
- xenobiology, astrobiology...

00:06:55.980 --> 00:06:58.330
There really are a lot
of sciences, aren't there?

00:06:58.373 --> 00:06:59.810
Too many if you ask me.

00:06:59.853 --> 00:07:01.725
Ah, it seems like
proper amount, but, uh,

00:07:01.768 --> 00:07:04.205
what I'm saying is, I think I'm
ready for the exam right now.

00:07:04.249 --> 00:07:06.512
Oh, well, according to this,
science officer training

00:07:06.556 --> 00:07:09.428
is less about tests and more
about learning to be, ooh,

00:07:09.472 --> 00:07:11.952
"the voice of science." Cute.

00:07:11.996 --> 00:07:13.911
But maybe it's, like,
also a test?

00:07:13.954 --> 00:07:15.826
'Cause I just really want
to take a test.

00:07:15.869 --> 00:07:18.742
Tendi, does it matter how much
you know if nobody's listening?

00:07:18.785 --> 00:07:21.266
Captains have big egos.
You need to cut through that

00:07:21.309 --> 00:07:23.181
and speak for science,

00:07:23.224 --> 00:07:26.184
which is why you will be serving
as a science officer trainee

00:07:26.227 --> 00:07:27.925
with Captain Freeman today.

00:07:27.968 --> 00:07:30.014
Isn't she busy
with an important negotiation?

00:07:30.057 --> 00:07:31.015
Exactly.

00:07:31.058 --> 00:07:32.451
I want you to focus

00:07:32.495 --> 00:07:34.279
on getting
the captain's attention.

00:07:34.322 --> 00:07:36.760
Really prove that you've got
the grapes to stand up to her.

00:07:36.803 --> 00:07:39.240
But won't that make her mad?

00:07:39.284 --> 00:07:40.894
Oh, definitely.

00:07:40.938 --> 00:07:42.809
Garçon, one more round of millet

00:07:42.853 --> 00:07:45.072
- and cut me off after that.

00:07:52.515 --> 00:07:54.386
Whoa.

00:07:54.429 --> 00:07:56.606
Hey, Samanthan,
you want to come over here

00:07:56.649 --> 00:07:59.391
and help me design some
Galaxy-class starship engines?

00:07:59.434 --> 00:08:02.350
Leah Brahms? No, man, no.

00:08:02.394 --> 00:08:04.439
Think about parrises squares,
think of parrises squares.

00:08:04.483 --> 00:08:05.789
This is your fantasy?

00:08:05.832 --> 00:08:08.487
Oh, yeah. Dr. Brahms
was instrumental

00:08:08.531 --> 00:08:09.793
in advancing warp field theory.

00:08:09.836 --> 00:08:11.316
I need a big brain engineer

00:08:11.359 --> 00:08:13.013
who can help me
extrude some plasma

00:08:13.057 --> 00:08:16.016
- and run some tests.
-  No! Leave me alone.

00:08:17.191 --> 00:08:18.976
Look at those stupid &lt;i&gt;
Carlsbad&lt;/i&gt; ensigns.

00:08:19.019 --> 00:08:20.455
What did they mean
"screw around"?

00:08:20.499 --> 00:08:21.892
Cali-class ships are all
practically the same.

00:08:21.935 --> 00:08:24.155
What the hell
are they so smug about?

00:08:24.198 --> 00:08:25.417
I mean, we have gotten into
some pretty notable shenanigans.

00:08:25.460 --> 00:08:27.201
Oh, please, like what?

00:08:27.245 --> 00:08:28.986
- We tussled with mugatos.
- Well, there was that Klingon

00:08:29.029 --> 00:08:30.335
- who took off in the ship
- We tussled with the Pakleds.

00:08:30.378 --> 00:08:32.032
- and he was drunk.
- Twice with the Pakleds.

00:08:32.076 --> 00:08:33.643
And we scared the crap out
of that drill instructor.

00:08:33.686 --> 00:08:35.209
Was there a thing
with time travel? Have we done

00:08:35.253 --> 00:08:36.515
- a time travel thing?
- Okay, okay, I get it,

00:08:36.559 --> 00:08:37.603
yeah, shenanigans.
You know what?

00:08:37.647 --> 00:08:38.343
Today, we're gonna do our job

00:08:38.386 --> 00:08:39.823
faster and better

00:08:39.866 --> 00:08:41.476
and kick their asses &lt;i&gt;
Cerritos&lt;/i&gt; style.

00:08:41.520 --> 00:08:43.217
I mean, we can try, but,
I mean, they're kind of amazing.

00:08:47.613 --> 00:08:49.093
What the... Did you see that?

00:08:49.136 --> 00:08:51.269
She's rubbing it in.
No, I'm the one who rubs. I rub.

00:08:51.312 --> 00:08:52.792
Okay, you know what,
you're right.

00:08:52.836 --> 00:08:54.620
Let's pick up the pace
and smoke these guys.

00:08:58.755 --> 00:09:00.060
- Come with me.

00:09:00.104 --> 00:09:02.193
We could increase
gravimetric power limits

00:09:02.236 --> 00:09:05.065
all... night... long.

00:09:05.109 --> 00:09:06.937
Rutherford, stay strong.
Parrises squares,

00:09:06.980 --> 00:09:09.548
ion mallet, shiny blue uniforms.
Come on.

00:09:09.592 --> 00:09:11.768
I can't believe
that's tempting to you.

00:09:11.811 --> 00:09:13.421
Yeah, these things'll
have to try a lot harder

00:09:13.465 --> 00:09:14.509
to get in my head.

00:09:14.553 --> 00:09:17.034
Ensign Boimler. There you are.

00:09:17.077 --> 00:09:19.079
Quick, get in, son.
The Borg are attacking.

00:09:19.123 --> 00:09:20.603
Starfleet needs
that Boimler magic.

00:09:20.646 --> 00:09:22.909
I knew
this day would come.

00:09:22.953 --> 00:09:24.694
Yes, sir, Admiral,
let's...

00:09:24.737 --> 00:09:27.305
- Dude, come on.
- Huh? Oh, geez, sorry.

00:09:27.348 --> 00:09:30.351
Also, a sidecar? Even in your
fantasy, you're not driving?

00:09:30.395 --> 00:09:32.310
Driving's scary.
I'm a natural passenger.

00:09:32.353 --> 00:09:34.921
Oh, hey, babe.

00:09:34.965 --> 00:09:36.575
I was about to go
yell at Ransom,

00:09:36.619 --> 00:09:38.708
really tear him a new one
for being so annoying.

00:09:38.751 --> 00:09:39.926
Want to come watch?

00:09:39.970 --> 00:09:41.406
Nice try, "babe,"
but I'll hold off

00:09:41.449 --> 00:09:43.234
for the real deal
back on the ship.

00:09:43.277 --> 00:09:45.366
Ho-ho-okay, you and Jennifer
are "babe-ing" each other now?

00:09:45.410 --> 00:09:46.846
Uh, yeah, I mean,
I guess we have been.

00:09:46.890 --> 00:09:48.543
Aw, it's nice to see you
with a girlfriend,

00:09:48.587 --> 00:09:50.415
instead of destroying everything
in your path.

00:09:50.458 --> 00:09:52.156
She's not my girlfriend.
We're just hanging out.

00:09:52.199 --> 00:09:54.767
- We're not into labels.
- Oh, I'm into labels.

00:09:54.811 --> 00:09:58.684
I'm fine being your
hot Andorian girlfriend.

00:09:58.728 --> 00:10:00.294
Is that your fantasy?

00:10:00.338 --> 00:10:02.470
No. Where-- No.
Go find Leah Brahms. Shut up.

00:10:02.514 --> 00:10:04.168
Ooh, somebody's blushing.

00:10:04.211 --> 00:10:06.910
I think she is.
I'm detecting an elevated

00:10:06.953 --> 00:10:08.738
- heart rate.
- Stop looking at my heart rate.

00:10:08.781 --> 00:10:10.653
Okay, we have to ignore these
totally inaccurate fantasies

00:10:10.696 --> 00:10:12.263
at all costs.

00:10:12.306 --> 00:10:13.786
Come and look at the warp core
with me and Leah.

00:10:16.615 --> 00:10:19.009
Huh, I had no idea
that Captain Maier

00:10:19.052 --> 00:10:20.837
was going to be so fresh-faced.

00:10:20.880 --> 00:10:22.882
What, he just graduate
from the Academy yesterday?

00:10:22.926 --> 00:10:24.579
I don't know, but word
around the fleet is that

00:10:24.623 --> 00:10:26.669
he's on the fast track
to a Galaxy-class.

00:10:26.712 --> 00:10:28.235
Uh, Captain.
I've been researching

00:10:28.279 --> 00:10:29.889
Captain Murakami's logs
about the Scrubble,

00:10:29.933 --> 00:10:31.412
and I think they are...

00:10:31.456 --> 00:10:32.805
- Captain Maier,

00:10:32.849 --> 00:10:34.807
your reputation precedes you.

00:10:34.851 --> 00:10:37.157
As does yours, Captain Freeman.

00:10:37.201 --> 00:10:39.507
I'm excited to learn from
how you close this deal today.

00:10:39.551 --> 00:10:42.119
Well, most of
the work's already been done.

00:10:42.162 --> 00:10:44.730
We just need to get everyone
to sign off on final points.

00:10:44.774 --> 00:10:45.905
Should only take
a minute or two.

00:10:45.949 --> 00:10:47.733
Still, it'll be good to see how

00:10:47.777 --> 00:10:49.343
the old school knocks this out.

00:10:49.387 --> 00:10:51.606
I'm sure we can do--
Wait, old school?

00:10:51.650 --> 00:10:53.652
Now hold on, hold on.
That is totally unfair.

00:10:53.696 --> 00:10:55.132
We had no idea that
the rocks we were studying

00:10:55.175 --> 00:10:56.916
had any silicate life.

00:10:56.960 --> 00:10:59.745
Well, what you call "silicate"
life, we just call "life."

00:10:59.789 --> 00:11:02.008
You do not seem alive to us.

00:11:02.052 --> 00:11:03.444
Everyone, everyone, please.

00:11:03.488 --> 00:11:05.185
Welcome to the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos.&lt;/i&gt;

00:11:05.229 --> 00:11:07.666
We have the treaty details
you've agreed to right here.

00:11:07.710 --> 00:11:08.972
Perhaps some refreshments?

00:11:09.015 --> 00:11:10.669
The Scrubble
thanks you, Captains.

00:11:10.713 --> 00:11:12.236
We appreciate the respect

00:11:12.279 --> 00:11:14.281
you both show the Scrubble,
unlike these

00:11:14.325 --> 00:11:16.066
- insolent scientists.
- Hey.

00:11:16.109 --> 00:11:18.329
May we present you
with a sacred

00:11:18.372 --> 00:11:20.461
- Scrubble totem?
- Oh, thank you so much.

00:11:20.505 --> 00:11:23.290
It's-it's lovely.
Captain Maier, please feel free

00:11:23.334 --> 00:11:25.902
to take this token of respect
for your collection.

00:11:25.945 --> 00:11:27.773
Oh, I couldn't possibly,
Captain Freeman.

00:11:27.817 --> 00:11:30.167
As the more senior officer,
the statue's all yours.

00:11:30.210 --> 00:11:32.909
Take the statue, young man.

00:11:32.952 --> 00:11:34.606
No, I couldn't impose.

00:11:34.649 --> 00:11:35.825
- Take it.
- No, you.

00:11:35.868 --> 00:11:37.391
- No, please. It's yours.
- Get it away.

00:11:37.435 --> 00:11:40.220
- Please let me help.

00:11:40.264 --> 00:11:42.353
I can make you
a captain, Boimler.

00:11:42.396 --> 00:11:45.704
- Can you triple-check my math?

00:11:49.621 --> 00:11:52.667
Nailed it, babe.
Let's make out.

00:11:52.711 --> 00:11:54.931
Yo, Kearns.
Five more, and we're done.

00:11:54.974 --> 00:11:56.454
Looks like you guys
have a ways to go, huh?

00:11:59.239 --> 00:12:01.241
What are you doing?
Come on,

00:12:01.285 --> 00:12:02.416
- pick it up.
- I think I pulled

00:12:02.460 --> 00:12:03.983
my dominant groin.

00:12:04.027 --> 00:12:06.420
This is great.
It's totally working.

00:12:06.464 --> 00:12:08.901
- Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.

00:12:08.945 --> 00:12:10.947
Did you just dunk
that fantasy rock?

00:12:10.990 --> 00:12:12.426
The hell were you thinking?

00:12:12.470 --> 00:12:14.167
Moving fast, sir.
Getting the job done.

00:12:14.211 --> 00:12:16.300
Well, slow it down.
These things are dangerous.

00:12:16.343 --> 00:12:18.215
They're not a bunch
of dang basketballs.

00:12:18.258 --> 00:12:20.217
Well, we just wanted
to make sure these &lt;i&gt;Carlsbad&lt;/i&gt; guys

00:12:20.260 --> 00:12:23.002
didn't outpace us and make
Commander Ransom look like

00:12:23.046 --> 00:12:24.221
an ineffectual leader.

00:12:24.264 --> 00:12:26.353
Ineffectual?
Why would they say that?

00:12:26.397 --> 00:12:28.355
Yeah, we overheard them saying
Ransom was a joke, and that

00:12:28.399 --> 00:12:30.531
his-his teams are slow,
and his core is weak.

00:12:30.575 --> 00:12:32.490
Bull[bleep]. He's got
the strongest core in the fleet.

00:12:32.533 --> 00:12:34.927
Now, hurry up. Let's move
some friggin' rocks.

00:12:34.971 --> 00:12:36.146
Let me show you how a pro

00:12:36.189 --> 00:12:37.887
does it. Whoa. Ooh!

00:12:39.497 --> 00:12:41.891
Uh, sir, what happens
if these things break?

00:12:41.934 --> 00:12:43.544
I'm sure it's fine.
It probably just makes

00:12:43.588 --> 00:12:45.198
a real big fantasy, right?

00:12:45.242 --> 00:12:48.332
Watch out,
giant ham sandwich incoming.

00:12:50.987 --> 00:12:52.989
Oh, my God. Kukulkan.

00:12:54.904 --> 00:12:58.124
My beautiful arms.

00:13:02.520 --> 00:13:03.913
What was that thing?

00:13:03.956 --> 00:13:05.697
Guys, I don't think
that was a fantasy.

00:13:05.740 --> 00:13:06.872
I think these broken rocks
are reading our nightmares.

00:13:06.916 --> 00:13:08.047
But I don't like my nightmares.

00:13:08.091 --> 00:13:10.093
What is that?

00:13:25.325 --> 00:13:27.110
In here, quick.

00:13:29.634 --> 00:13:30.940
- Wow.

00:13:30.983 --> 00:13:33.725
Good aim is hot.

00:13:35.205 --> 00:13:37.903
JENNIFER'S VOICE: I want
to be exclusive! I want us

00:13:37.947 --> 00:13:40.079
to grow old and boring and grow

00:13:40.123 --> 00:13:41.994
orchids together, babe.

00:13:47.739 --> 00:13:50.655
Settle down with me!

00:13:50.698 --> 00:13:52.004
- Whew.
- Mariner,

00:13:52.048 --> 00:13:53.614
you might want
to go back to therapy.

00:13:56.879 --> 00:13:59.055
&lt;i&gt;- Cerritos,&lt;/i&gt; come in.

00:13:59.098 --> 00:14:01.405
Of course. It's not
a real day in Starfleet

00:14:01.448 --> 00:14:02.972
till comms get blocked.

00:14:03.015 --> 00:14:04.321
Okay, how long before
these things dissipate?

00:14:04.364 --> 00:14:06.584
With those psychic mines broken,
who knows?

00:14:06.627 --> 00:14:07.890
We'll have to wait it out.

00:14:07.933 --> 00:14:09.456
We are trapped
in a cave,

00:14:09.500 --> 00:14:11.154
and your commander is armless.

00:14:11.197 --> 00:14:12.938
I fear we will be
penalized for this.

00:14:12.982 --> 00:14:15.071
No, I will. I made us rush.

00:14:15.114 --> 00:14:16.420
Why? We had all day.

00:14:16.463 --> 00:14:17.856
You guys were going so fast,

00:14:17.900 --> 00:14:19.727
we-we were trying
to speed up to beat you.

00:14:19.771 --> 00:14:22.382
It's clear the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos&lt;/i&gt;
has a bad reputation.

00:14:22.426 --> 00:14:23.993
We didn't want to live up to it.

00:14:24.036 --> 00:14:26.952
Wow. I'm speechless.

00:14:26.996 --> 00:14:29.259
Come on, don't pile on.
Look, the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos&lt;/i&gt; is actually

00:14:29.302 --> 00:14:31.043
a really great place to serve...

00:14:31.087 --> 00:14:32.740
No, no, I mean, we were
the ones who were rushing.

00:14:32.784 --> 00:14:33.741
What?

00:14:33.785 --> 00:14:35.352
You guys are so cool,

00:14:35.395 --> 00:14:37.049
and we were just
trying to impress you.

00:14:37.093 --> 00:14:38.877
Wait, you think we're cool?

00:14:38.921 --> 00:14:41.924
Yes. The tales of your exploits
are widely shared.

00:14:41.967 --> 00:14:45.144
The &lt;i&gt;Cerritos&lt;/i&gt; is,
in fact, the coolest.

00:14:45.188 --> 00:14:46.667
&lt;i&gt;
Collecting stuff isn't really&lt;/i&gt;

00:14:46.711 --> 00:14:48.321
&lt;i&gt;a thing with my generation.&lt;/i&gt;

00:14:48.365 --> 00:14:51.063
No disrespect, I just don't need
flashy trinkets to...

00:14:51.107 --> 00:14:52.891
It's a normal rock.

00:14:52.935 --> 00:14:55.372
Ensign, come here, scan this
thing and tell Captain Maier

00:14:55.415 --> 00:14:57.026
- it's not flashy.

00:14:57.069 --> 00:14:58.636
Hmm, it has an anomalous

00:14:58.679 --> 00:15:00.159
molecular composition.
I'm actually

00:15:00.203 --> 00:15:01.813
getting some pretty
interesting readings...

00:15:01.856 --> 00:15:03.119
Stop talking.
It's clearly not fancy.

00:15:03.162 --> 00:15:05.512
Ah-ha-ha, see, there you go.

00:15:05.556 --> 00:15:07.253
A "pretty interesting" object

00:15:07.297 --> 00:15:08.689
for a pretty
experienced captain.

00:15:08.733 --> 00:15:10.213
Captains, captains,

00:15:10.256 --> 00:15:12.432
maybe we should get to business,
what do you say?

00:15:12.476 --> 00:15:14.173
- Take the rock. No, no.
- You take it.

00:15:14.217 --> 00:15:15.827
- Don't you dare. No, no.
- It's a gift.

00:15:15.870 --> 00:15:18.308
- Just take it. Take it!
- Just take the rock!

00:15:19.787 --> 00:15:22.616
Oh, yeah, all the Cali-class
crews talk about the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos.&lt;/i&gt;

00:15:22.660 --> 00:15:24.662
You guys are famous.

00:15:24.705 --> 00:15:26.751
Famous? Us? [chuckles] No way.

00:15:26.794 --> 00:15:28.840
Come on, the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos&lt;/i&gt; is like

00:15:28.883 --> 00:15:30.755
the &lt;i&gt;Enterprise&lt;/i&gt;
of the support ships.

00:15:30.798 --> 00:15:32.887
You have survived battles
with the Pakleds.

00:15:32.931 --> 00:15:35.890
You four stood strong
in an alien trial.

00:15:35.934 --> 00:15:37.936
Eh, it was more of a party,
but thanks.

00:15:37.980 --> 00:15:40.547
All the other Cali-class ships
just do what they're told,

00:15:40.591 --> 00:15:42.593
but the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos&lt;/i&gt; kicks ass.

00:15:42.636 --> 00:15:44.899
We kind of freaked out
when we got this mission.

00:15:44.943 --> 00:15:47.032
We just wanted to show you
that we could keep up.

00:15:47.076 --> 00:15:49.904
You did more than keep
up. You guys were crushing it.

00:15:53.430 --> 00:15:56.607
Give us your distinctiveness.

00:15:57.782 --> 00:15:59.001
What?

00:16:03.048 --> 00:16:05.572
- You're scared of basketballs?
- I'm not.

00:16:05.616 --> 00:16:07.705
So, your greatest fantasy
is basketball?

00:16:07.748 --> 00:16:09.924
No, I hadn't heard the word
"basketball" in years

00:16:09.968 --> 00:16:12.579
until Stevens said it just
before the nightmares showed up.

00:16:12.623 --> 00:16:15.234
I guess the stones must've
pulled that from my mind, too?

00:16:15.278 --> 00:16:16.670
Fantasies and fears I get,

00:16:16.714 --> 00:16:18.672
but why access that part
of your brain?

00:16:18.716 --> 00:16:21.327
Uh, there's a bunch of stuff out
there that doesn't make sense.

00:16:21.371 --> 00:16:23.721
Hey, babe.

00:16:23.764 --> 00:16:25.070
Does Jennifer wear hats?

00:16:25.114 --> 00:16:26.724
No, her antennae
are too sensitive.

00:16:26.767 --> 00:16:29.422
But I did overhear
Levy mansplaining

00:16:29.466 --> 00:16:31.076
the difference between
a pork pie and a fedora

00:16:31.120 --> 00:16:32.773
to some poor cadet
the other day.

00:16:32.817 --> 00:16:35.037
These stones are recording
way more than we thought.

00:16:35.080 --> 00:16:38.040
Something in here is streaming
a ton of data.

00:16:38.083 --> 00:16:39.606
Whatever's receiving it

00:16:39.650 --> 00:16:41.652
is back there.

00:16:45.743 --> 00:16:48.528
Give it to me straight,
Doc, is it bad?

00:16:48.572 --> 00:16:51.705
You're fine, just relax.
I need a sedative over here.

00:16:51.749 --> 00:16:53.098
Here you go, Doctor.

00:16:53.142 --> 00:16:54.143
What the
are you doing here?

00:16:54.186 --> 00:16:55.535
Weren't you supposed to start

00:16:55.579 --> 00:16:56.710
science officer stuff
with Migleemo?

00:16:56.754 --> 00:16:59.104
Yup, first day.
It's going great.

00:16:59.148 --> 00:17:01.498
-  the bed, huh?
- Yes, I think that's accurate.

00:17:01.541 --> 00:17:03.413
- Aw, geez, are you about to cry?

00:17:03.456 --> 00:17:05.589
This guy's not even crying, and
his toes are getting digested.

00:17:05.632 --> 00:17:06.590
They are?

00:17:06.633 --> 00:17:08.200
Shut up, don't move.

00:17:08.244 --> 00:17:10.637
I just don't know if I'm cut out
to be a science officer.

00:17:10.681 --> 00:17:12.465
I can't get the captain
to listen to me.

00:17:12.509 --> 00:17:14.380
Okay,
guess we're doing this.

00:17:14.424 --> 00:17:16.469
Tendi, of course
you're cut out for it.

00:17:16.513 --> 00:17:17.775
That's why I recommended you.

00:17:17.818 --> 00:17:19.168
Then why am I blowing it?

00:17:19.211 --> 00:17:20.908
All my studying
hasn't helped at all.

00:17:20.952 --> 00:17:22.823
No, no, studying's good,
but in real life

00:17:22.867 --> 00:17:24.912
there's gonna be times when you
need to make a mess of things

00:17:24.956 --> 00:17:26.610
before you can fix them.

00:17:26.653 --> 00:17:28.307
Like how I'm gonna have
to cut this guy's foot off,

00:17:28.351 --> 00:17:30.135
- so we can grow him a new one.
- Wait, what was that?

00:17:30.179 --> 00:17:32.616
You'll be a great officer on
the bridge one day, but you're

00:17:32.659 --> 00:17:34.748
gonna have to risk
screwing things up to get there.

00:17:34.792 --> 00:17:37.229
- You understand?
- I do. Thanks, Doc.

00:17:37.273 --> 00:17:39.362
- Good luck growing it back.
- Hey,

00:17:39.405 --> 00:17:40.667
so you were just kidding
about my foot

00:17:40.711 --> 00:17:42.104
to make a point, right?

00:17:47.761 --> 00:17:50.199
Cave bug.
We've got cave bugs in here.

00:17:50.242 --> 00:17:52.723
Wait, look,
I think this is a door.

00:17:52.766 --> 00:17:55.117
Huh, that's not a usual thing
for a cave.

00:17:55.160 --> 00:17:57.162
Hey, there's an access panel
over here.

00:18:00.644 --> 00:18:03.255
Whoa, what is this place?

00:18:03.299 --> 00:18:05.562
Don't know, but this
is definitely the receiver.

00:18:05.605 --> 00:18:08.130
And some kind of storage device.

00:18:09.348 --> 00:18:11.307
- Look.
- It's storing all our thoughts.

00:18:11.350 --> 00:18:13.744
It has our security clearances, passwords,

00:18:13.787 --> 00:18:15.441
personal information.

00:18:15.485 --> 00:18:18.401
My Uncle Trent drunk-dancing
at my cousin's wedding.

00:18:18.444 --> 00:18:19.750
Damn. Get it, Trent.

00:18:19.793 --> 00:18:21.273
This thing is
a literal data mine.

00:18:21.317 --> 00:18:22.927
Whoa, whoa, whoa,
but look at the equipment.

00:18:22.970 --> 00:18:24.494
It's all Federation tech.

00:18:24.537 --> 00:18:26.931
The outpost scientists
must have installed it. But why?

00:18:26.974 --> 00:18:28.628
Unless they
and the Scrubble are...

00:18:28.672 --> 00:18:30.935
- Working together.
- We should probably

00:18:30.978 --> 00:18:32.850
- report this, huh?
- Big-time.

00:18:32.893 --> 00:18:35.244
Hey, you think there's any
chance the crazy crystal cavern

00:18:35.287 --> 00:18:36.941
is maybe boosting comms?
I don't know.

00:18:36.984 --> 00:18:38.595
- Yeah, no, of course not.

00:18:38.638 --> 00:18:40.249
Well, you guys lucked out.

00:18:40.292 --> 00:18:42.555
You're getting the full &lt;i&gt;
Cerritos&lt;/i&gt; experience today.

00:18:59.398 --> 00:19:01.052
- Die!

00:19:01.095 --> 00:19:02.923
- Kearns to &lt;i&gt;Carlsbad.&lt;/i&gt;
- Boimler to &lt;i&gt;Cerritos.&lt;/i&gt;

00:19:02.967 --> 00:19:04.751
- Oh, I'm sorry, do you want...
- I'm sorry, did I step on...?

00:19:04.795 --> 00:19:06.536
- We need emergency-- Wow.
- Requesting immediate-- O-Okay.

00:19:06.579 --> 00:19:07.885
- I can, I can walk over there.
-  Are you sure?

00:19:07.928 --> 00:19:09.060
It's okay.
No, no, it's-it's fine.

00:19:14.892 --> 00:19:16.502
- Just take it!
- No, you take it!

00:19:16.546 --> 00:19:18.504
How about if we split it? Shaxs,
phaser this thing in half.

00:19:18.548 --> 00:19:19.940
- Now we're talking.
- How dare you?

00:19:19.984 --> 00:19:21.464
This is a sacred gift.

00:19:21.507 --> 00:19:23.074
Why don't we just
go back down to the planet

00:19:23.117 --> 00:19:24.249
and get another one?

00:19:24.293 --> 00:19:25.946
No. I'm running
the negotiations,

00:19:25.990 --> 00:19:28.645
- and I say Maier gets the rock.
- And as your guest,

00:19:28.688 --> 00:19:30.734
- I decline.
- What is wrong with you?

00:19:30.777 --> 00:19:32.083
Just take the thing and stick it

00:19:32.126 --> 00:19:33.911
in the closet
like everybody else.

00:19:33.954 --> 00:19:34.825
I'm not gonna be the captain
who wouldn't let Carol Freeman

00:19:34.868 --> 00:19:36.566
have a peace treaty gift.

00:19:36.609 --> 00:19:37.741
- I don't need it.
- If someone doesn't take it,

00:19:37.784 --> 00:19:39.221
we're not signing the treaty.

00:19:39.264 --> 00:19:40.483
Someone just take
the damn thing,

00:19:40.526 --> 00:19:41.571
so we can get this over with!

00:19:41.614 --> 00:19:43.094
Everybody stop yelling!

00:19:43.137 --> 00:19:44.617
- I'm having flashbacks.
- Hold on.

00:19:44.661 --> 00:19:46.053
Everyone, stop, stop, stop.
We just got back

00:19:46.097 --> 00:19:47.403
from the planet.
You have to stop this.

00:19:47.446 --> 00:19:48.795
Mariner,
what the hell are you doing?

00:19:48.839 --> 00:19:50.144
It's true, Commander,
we scanned...

00:19:50.188 --> 00:19:50.667
Just take the rock,
take the rock.

00:19:50.710 --> 00:19:51.320
Shut up!

00:19:52.582 --> 00:19:54.323
Ensign, have you lost your mind?

00:19:54.366 --> 00:19:56.325
Look at the damn rock.

00:19:56.368 --> 00:19:59.719
Is that... Federation tech?

00:19:59.763 --> 00:20:01.504
Those anomalous readings?

00:20:01.547 --> 00:20:03.288
- It's an internal power source.
- Tendi's right.

00:20:03.332 --> 00:20:04.550
These guys are working together.

00:20:04.594 --> 00:20:05.899
They have
a whole system down there

00:20:05.943 --> 00:20:07.205
where they read minds
using rocks

00:20:07.249 --> 00:20:09.163
and store it
with Federation systems.

00:20:09.207 --> 00:20:10.861
A spy device?

00:20:10.904 --> 00:20:12.950
And you both wanted it planted
in a captain's office.

00:20:12.993 --> 00:20:16.432
They would have heard top secret
communications, deployments.

00:20:16.475 --> 00:20:19.043
Well, this is, uh, preposterous.

00:20:19.086 --> 00:20:20.827
I-I want to go back to my cave
this instant.

00:20:20.871 --> 00:20:24.222
Yes, yes, and I have important
work to do at the outpost,

00:20:24.266 --> 00:20:25.745
- groundbreaking stuff.

00:20:25.789 --> 00:20:27.443
- Actually,

00:20:27.486 --> 00:20:29.836
I think I'm finally ready
to start this meeting.

00:20:31.664 --> 00:20:33.971
Great plan, genius.

00:20:35.625 --> 00:20:37.322
&lt;i&gt;
Captain's log, supplemental.&lt;/i&gt;

00:20:37.366 --> 00:20:38.976
&lt;i&gt;The animosity
between the Scrubble&lt;/i&gt;

00:20:39.019 --> 00:20:40.847
&lt;i&gt;and Outpost 76 scientists&lt;/i&gt;

00:20:40.891 --> 00:20:42.806
&lt;i&gt;was a manufactured deception,&lt;/i&gt;

00:20:42.849 --> 00:20:45.635
&lt;i&gt;designed to distract from
their plan to collect and sell&lt;/i&gt;

00:20:45.678 --> 00:20:48.942
&lt;i&gt;sensitive Starfleet intelligence
on the black market.&lt;/i&gt;

00:20:48.986 --> 00:20:50.292
Apparently,
the scientists wanted

00:20:50.335 --> 00:20:51.815
to purchase better equipment,

00:20:51.858 --> 00:20:54.731
and the Scrubble
wanted more... rocks?

00:20:54.774 --> 00:20:57.429
I don't get how that
would-- Whatever. Anyway,

00:20:57.473 --> 00:20:59.910
they'll both be answering
to a Federation tribunal.

00:20:59.953 --> 00:21:02.216
In recognition of their
excellent teamwork,

00:21:02.260 --> 00:21:05.307
&lt;i&gt;Captain Maier and I have
authorized a small celebration&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:05.350 --> 00:21:07.004
&lt;i&gt;for our combined crews.&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:07.047 --> 00:21:08.745
I was, like,
"Okay, Doc,

00:21:08.788 --> 00:21:10.660
"if I was brain dead
for ten minutes,

00:21:10.703 --> 00:21:12.444
"then how come I saw a koala

00:21:12.488 --> 00:21:14.272
sitting on a black mount...?"
Wait. Where are you going?

00:21:14.316 --> 00:21:16.013
Okay.

00:21:16.056 --> 00:21:17.928
Looks like it's just
you and me, old friend.

00:21:17.971 --> 00:21:20.583
Gah, cinnamon schnapps.

00:21:20.626 --> 00:21:23.237
Innkeeper,
two Grimpari Sun Storms,

00:21:23.281 --> 00:21:25.718
one for me
and one for my mentee,

00:21:25.762 --> 00:21:27.372
who made sure she was heard.

00:21:27.416 --> 00:21:30.723
I couldn't have done it
without a great mentor.

00:21:30.767 --> 00:21:32.377
Why, thank you, Tendi.

00:21:32.421 --> 00:21:35.206
I must admit, this new role
rather suits me.

00:21:35.249 --> 00:21:36.947
A toast, to me.

00:21:36.990 --> 00:21:39.558
And, to a lesser extent,
but also worth noting, Tendi.

00:21:40.777 --> 00:21:44.171
Carol, I need to
apologize for my behavior today.

00:21:44.215 --> 00:21:45.651
I-I hope you don't
think less of me.

00:21:45.695 --> 00:21:47.261
Well, you and the &lt;i&gt;Carlsbad&lt;/i&gt; team

00:21:47.305 --> 00:21:48.567
impressed the hell out of me.

00:21:48.611 --> 00:21:50.613
In fact, I got you something.

00:21:50.656 --> 00:21:51.962
But this is gonna record my...

00:21:52.005 --> 00:21:53.790
Don't worry,
it's been neutralized.

00:21:53.833 --> 00:21:56.096
I know you think collecting
trinkets is old-school, but...

00:21:56.140 --> 00:21:59.143
I would be honored.
Are you sure you don't want it?

00:21:59.186 --> 00:22:00.710
Please, that's the little half.

00:22:00.753 --> 00:22:02.625
I kept the big one for myself.

00:22:04.496 --> 00:22:07.456
You guys really lived up
to your reputations today.

00:22:07.499 --> 00:22:09.806
Wow, we had no idea anyone
talked about the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos.&lt;/i&gt;

00:22:09.849 --> 00:22:11.590
Oh, maybe not across the fleet,

00:22:11.634 --> 00:22:13.984
but you're definitely
Cali-class famous.

00:22:14.027 --> 00:22:15.289
Really? What do they say?

00:22:15.333 --> 00:22:17.422
Mariner's an unstoppable
force of nature.

00:22:17.466 --> 00:22:18.771
- Truth.
- Rutherford's a genius

00:22:18.815 --> 00:22:20.077
with crazy implant powers.

00:22:20.120 --> 00:22:21.208
- Okey dokey.
- Tendi's a ray

00:22:21.252 --> 00:22:22.775
- of optimistic sunshine.
- Aw.

00:22:22.819 --> 00:22:25.212
The only thing people
get wrong is Boimler.

00:22:25.256 --> 00:22:27.606
Let me guess, everyone thinks
I'm older, right?

00:22:27.650 --> 00:22:30.696
No, in stories you're described
as a tiny comedic robot

00:22:30.740 --> 00:22:32.089
that is always
getting into trouble.

00:22:32.132 --> 00:22:33.482
Wait, wait, wait,
what do they say?

00:22:33.525 --> 00:22:35.048
- Yes, that is so accurate.

00:22:35.092 --> 00:22:36.876
- No, it's not.
- I expected you to be, like,

00:22:36.920 --> 00:22:38.400
a hovering cube or something.

00:22:38.443 --> 00:22:40.097
Guys, you got to tell people
I'm a man.

00:22:40.140 --> 00:22:41.533
Oh, no, no. Please keep telling
people he's a cube.

00:22:41.577 --> 00:22:43.187
Mariner, no. Don't do that.

00:22:43.230 --> 00:22:45.058
:
Aw, Boimler wants to be people.

00:22:45.102 --> 00:22:47.409
&lt;i&gt;Guys, please,
please tell them I'm people.&lt;/i&gt;

00:22:47.452 --> 00:22:49.672
&lt;i&gt;Guys, I'm people!&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:49.122 --> 00:23:53.122
Chirp.
